    "body": "first slice on issue/1120-theme-colour-tokens · PR #3990 (`Refs #1120`, draft) · pinned by `colour_literals::no_colour_literal_outside_the_allowed_rows`\n\nThe PR adds only the guard. It changes no colour. A literal is a named constant (`Color32::WHITE`) or a constructor whose arguments are all numbers written in place. A constructor over variables (`from_rgb(r, g, b)`) converts a colour chosen elsewhere and does not count. On `main` at f287a370c there are 142 colour literals in 24 files. About 105 of them are sites to move; the estimate of 2026-11-12 said 51. Each row of the allow-list says why it stays, or which family PR moves it. Colour data kept as plain numbers (the G-code syntax table, `PICK_RGB8`) is not seen by the guard; the family PRs move it by name.\n\nThe family PRs that follow, each `Refs #1120`, the last `Fixes #1120`:\n\n1. Viewport overlays, in three PRs: handle and pick inks; ground ink, view cube and viewport bar; generate overlay, drop hint and shell overlays.\n2. Tool drawings (tool, holder and profile previews, tool library views).\n3. Verdict palettes (`colorvision.rs`): into the token table, values unchanged.\n4. G-code syntax colours, window chrome and status inks.\n\nEach family adds its tokens to the dark and light tables and to the theme-file keys, and lowers its rows in the guard.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
